.Dd October 1, 2026
.Dt GOLDIN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm goldin
.Nd Divide an HFS or HFS+ two-fork file into a data fork and an AppleDouble
encoded resource fork
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h , Fl \-help , Fl u
.Op Fl s , Fl \-strip
.Op Fl v , Fl \-verbose
.Op Fl \-norecurse
.Op Fl \-version
.Ar PATH ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Goldin does the same job as
.Xr SplitForks 1
with some enhanced functionality.
It converts Macintosh HFS or HFS Extended ("HFS+") two-fork files into
AppleDouble format with the data fork and the resource fork plus file system
metadata in separate files.
The original SplitForks only acted on one file.
Goldin accepts one or more paths, and will search any directory passed to it
recursively for files to convert, unless
.Fl \-norecurse
is given.
.Pp
Each
.Ar PATH
is split itself as well as its contents, so a folder with Finder information
gets its own AppleDouble file alongside it, in its parent folder.
.Pp
Paths are processed in turn.
Folders that cannot be read, including a
.Ar PATH
itself, are reported and skipped, and processing continues.
Any other error is reported and stops goldin without processing the
remaining paths.
.Pp
.Nm
accepts these options and arguments:
.Bl -tag -width -indent
.It Fl h , Fl \-help , Fl u
Print usage information and exit.
.Fl u
is kept for backwards compatibility.
.It Fl s , Fl \-strip
Strip the resource fork from the original file.
The default is to leave the resource fork in place after copying it to its
AppleDouble metadata file.
.It Fl v , Fl \-verbose
Verbose mode.
Prints to standard output when a file is to be split.
.It Fl \-norecurse
Only split the files and folders directly inside each
.Ar PATH ;
don't descend into its subdirectories.
.It Fl \-version
Print the tool's version and exit.
.It Ar PATH ...
One or more files or directories to split.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width -indent
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/goldin
The installed tool.
.It example
A file to convert.
.It example.d/
A directory to search for files to convert.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 2
An unknown option was given.
.It 254
A
.Ar PATH
is not on an HFS or HFS+ volume.
.It 255
Any other error, including no
.Ar PATH
being given.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Goldin will fail with an error if a file or directory is not on an HFS or
HFS+ volume.
.Pp
Unless goldin is run as root, the AppleDouble files it creates are owned by
the user running it.
Only the permissions of the original file are copied, not its owner or group.
.Pp
Goldin lives here:
.Lk https://github.com/packagesdev/goldin .
.Pp
To know why this tool is named goldin, see
.Lk https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sawing_a_woman_in_half
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr FixupResourceForks 1 ,
.Xr goldout 1 ,
.Xr SplitForks 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 1740 documents AppleSingle/AppleDouble formats.